subQuestions.questionText:
Indicate whether the following statement is TRUE or FALSE:

The value 23 will be displayed in the rich edit component when the following code is executed:

    var
      arrNumbers : array[1..5] of Integer = (4,2,3,1,8);
      iValue : Integer;
    begin
      iValue := arrNumbers[2]+ arrNumbers[3];
      redOutput.Lines.Add(intToStr(iValue));
    end;

A group of friends throws a six-sided dice three times to decide what type of meal they will have. Rules: if the first throw is larger than the second throw, they eat chicken; else if the third throw is less than the first throw, they eat fish; else they eat burgers. The following incomplete Delphi solution is provided:

    var
      iFirst, iSecond, iThird : Integer;
      sMeal : string;
    begin
      iFirst  := Inputbox('Enter value of first throw', '', '');
      iSecond := Inputbox('Enter value of second throw', '', '');
      iThird  := Inputbox('Enter value of third throw', '', '');
      // Complete the program (Question 5.3.2)
      showMessage(sMeal);
    end.

Explain why a syntax error will be displayed when the provided part of the program is executed.
